WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.600
This video is dedicated to two different types
of people.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.680
One, you're either not an entrepreneur - and
I'm going to make a case why you out to become

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:15.181
an entrepreneur - and two, you may be an entrepreneur
and you've forgotten why you became an entrepreneur

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.360
in the first place.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.759
So let's get right into it.

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:25.420
26 why you ought to become an entrepreneur,
in no specific order.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:31.880
#1: The Unknown - there's something exciting
about becoming an entrepreneur because every

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.730
day there's an unknown.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.440
What's going to happen with this?

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.510
What if this takes place?

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.510
What if that takes place?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.120
And it needs to prepare you for certain things.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.120
You need to bring out a certain side of you
that you've never seen before.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.680
That's the unknown.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.620
The unknown part brings out a certain unpredictable
side of you that you can only see if you're

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.620
an entrepreneur.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.000
And being an employee, you know, it's pretty
much, "Hey, we're doing this" - unless you're

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.870
in an environment that's constantly growing,
for the most part, most people it's every

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.190
day it's the same exact thing.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.309
So #1, is unknown.

00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:05.740
#2:Constantly having to meet a newer, better
version of yourself.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.740
So think about this.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.950
Think about you're 30 years old, watching
this.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:14.350
If you're an entrepreneur, and you don't recreate
yourself every 90 days, you aren't going to

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.410
make it as an entrepreneur.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.190
You're going to get crushed by somebody else.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.610
If you aren't constantly improving yourself,
you're going to get hammered by somebody else.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:25.540
So the great thing about becoming an entrepreneur
and you're 30, imagine what you're going to

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:26.650
be at 31.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.330
That's exciting!

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:34.550
Imagine what you're going to be at 32, at
33, 34, oh my God, 40, 45, 48, 50!

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.740
Man, how am I going to be at 50?

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.520
You may be watching this and you're 17.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.470
How will you be at 22?

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.500
How will you be at 27?

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.810
At 29?

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.580
That's the exciting part of seeing a better
version of you.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:55.550
It's like an award-winning movie you're watching
that every time I'm going to be the new character,

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.100
but the entire character is who?

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.100
You.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.140
#3: Freedom - you have the freedom to do a
lot of different things.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.470
Freedom is a big part of it.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.730
Most people don't have the freedom that they
want when you have a job.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.591
The freedom could be making as much money
as you want to make, freedom to travel, see

00:02:09.591 --> 00:02:12.450
the world, freedom to where you want to live,
zip code, all this other stuff.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.749
It's freedom.

00:02:13.749 --> 00:02:16.430
#4: It's the greatest game you'll ever play.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.609
So if you're watching this and say, "I love
video games."

00:02:18.609 --> 00:02:20.560
For some people that love video games.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.230
If you're watching this, "I love board games."

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.079
What are some of the board games we play?

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:27.800
Monopoly, what else is there?

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:38.170
Chess, Life, or Clue, Monopoly -- I mean,
these things are games because it's like how

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.319
can I win in this game?

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:43.349
Becoming an entrepreneur is the greatest board
game you'll ever play.

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:44.420
Let me tell you.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.680
There's not a better board game than being.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:51.610
. . mark my words, there's not a better board
game than becoming an entrepreneur, because

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:55.701
it's a game you're playing, there's a score,
there's excitement, there's strategy, there's

00:02:55.701 --> 00:03:01.459
team partnership, collaboration, it's exciting
when you're running a game for the rest of

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:04.719
your life, and can you imagine playing a game
for 50 more years?

00:03:04.719 --> 00:03:06.620
That's becoming an entrepreneur.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.480
#5:No politics.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.620
When I say no politics, look, no matter what
you ever do, there's going to be some level

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.620
of politics.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:18.939
But in the world of business, as an entrepreneur,
if you kind of want to do what you want to

00:03:18.939 --> 00:03:19.939
do, there's a lot of things you can do.

00:03:19.939 --> 00:03:20.939
You have flexibility.

00:03:20.939 --> 00:03:24.599
Now is it smart to go around and telling everybody
off all the time?

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:25.599
Of course not.

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:27.379
Then you're not creating synergistic relationships.

00:03:27.379 --> 00:03:32.129
But you don't have the politics of I better
do this before I move up and I have to kiss

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.390
his butt before I move up.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:36.480
There is none of that going on in the world
of entrepreneurship.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.989
#6: Get paid what you're worth.

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:38.989
What do you want to make?

00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:39.989
You're going to get paid.

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:42.390
By the way, if you're an entrepreneur and
you're saying, "Well, you know, I only make

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.700
$30,000 a year as an entrepreneur."

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.840
That's what you're worth today, based on your
effort, improvement, progress, innovation,

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.359
thinking, creativity, work ethic, all of that
stuff.

00:03:51.359 --> 00:03:54.719
If you're an entrepreneur making 2 million
dollars a year right now, guess what you're

00:03:54.719 --> 00:03:55.719
worth?

00:03:55.719 --> 00:03:57.540
You are worth 2 million dollars a year as
an entrepreneur.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.519
#7: You're fireproof.

00:03:59.519 --> 00:04:00.959
What's fireproof?

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:02.370
No one can fire you.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:06.340
The only people that can fire you are your
customers and your employees.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.700
But everybody else, no one can come and say,
you're fired today.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:10.700
Nope.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:11.700
You can't get fired.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:12.700
There's no one that can fire you.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.849
You're fireproof.

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:16.310
#8: Happiness.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:21.720
Generally, you meet bitter people, bitter
people are simply coming from a state of not

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.720
improving.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.800
If somebody doesn't improve, they're bitter.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:30.560
You meet happy people, they're typically improving
and they're typically creating.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.099
Bitter people don't improve, don't create,
Happy people improve and create.

00:04:35.099 --> 00:04:39.669
There's a certain level of high you get when
you're improving and you're creating.

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:40.960
Happiness comes from that.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.360
You know, a lot of people say, "My gosh, why
are entrepreneurs so fired up and energized?"

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.711
You go try to create an improve and see what
happens to you.

00:04:47.711 --> 00:04:49.910
You'll be very happy yourself as well.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.259
#9: You don't have to be a genius.

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:55.319
You know, you do not have to be a genius to
make it as an entrepreneur.

00:04:55.319 --> 00:04:56.319
Why?

00:04:56.319 --> 00:04:58.160
You can always recruit geniuses.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:01.349
You can always recruit people that are 10
times smarter than you.

00:05:01.349 --> 00:05:04.030
Sometimes in the corporate world, you have
to be a genius to move up, but you have to

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.679
do a lot of things to move up, and all these
fancy.

00:05:05.679 --> 00:05:08.560
. . you don't have to worry about that as
an entrepreneur.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:14.080
You can simply be a very good recruiter of
genius minds and then that helps you grow

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.840
as an entrepreneur.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.660
#10: It's the closest thing you'll play to
sports.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.199
So if you love sports, and you're a person
that loves your football or baseball or basketball

00:05:23.199 --> 00:05:27.909
or swimming or soccer or hockey, whatever
it is, and you played high school football

00:05:27.909 --> 00:05:31.580
or high school basketball, college maybe,
or you were professional for some of you guys

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.890
that are professional sports that you follow
me and we talk about it all the time, and

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:41.289
afterwards, if you've played competitive sports,
and that part is missing - man, it's as if

00:05:41.289 --> 00:05:42.950
a part of you died.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:43.950
Literally.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.599
It's as if a part of you died.

00:05:46.599 --> 00:05:52.770
If you played sports and there's no more sports
or competition, it's the sports of business.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:57.810
Similar things take place -- practice, putting
a team together, competition, leaders, stats,

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:03.819
showing up early, leaving late, hitting the
weights, all of that is combined together

00:06:03.819 --> 00:06:05.430
because it's the closest thing you'll play
to sports.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.430
#11: Creativity.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:12.699
You can use your creativity in so many different
ways - strategies, marketing, creating an

00:06:12.699 --> 00:06:21.590
edge, product, events, sales, contests - so
many different ways you can use your creativity.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:25.100
#12: Community - you're part of a community.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.490
You're part of a community of other entrepreneurs.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.220
You speak a certain language that other entrepreneurs
speak.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:34.210
Have you ever gone to a certain city or certain
country and they speak a different language

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.820
